WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:01.273
- Hey, I'm Kane.

00:00:01.273 --> 00:00:03.390
A couple months ago, I
helped Kristin from Ladylike

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:04.610
redecorate her desk.

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:06.110
You all seemed really into it.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.560
After that, I helped Freddie
redecorate her bedroom space

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:12.890
so she could spend more
stress-free time in there.

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:15.360
I really do believe that
we'd all be a little happier

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.610
if we had our own versions of an oasis

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:18.720
that we could go home to.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.070
Today I'm meeting up with Melina,

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.240
who wanted help redesigning
her living space

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.540
for her adult son who
happens to have autism.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.253
Come on, check it out!

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.353
This is your new living room.

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:29.810
- [Melina] Oh my goodness!

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:31.340
- She wanted help figuring out

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.700
how to make their space uniquely adult

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.070
and hopefully help them transition

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.830
into the new phases of their lives.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:38.910
- My name is Melina Fernandez-Burn,

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.910
and I'm a mom, and I
have two boys, 18 and 21.

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:45.060
As a mom, you think they're
gonna be children forever.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:46.520
Now that they really are adults,

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.460
it would be a great way
to bring in the new phases

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:50.310
of adult life.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:53.983
It is just a special time
of coming into your own.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.163
- What is autism?

00:00:55.163 --> 00:00:58.100
- Autism is a neurological
developmental disorder.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.130
It doesn't mean they have low cognition.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:02.330
It just means, if they're on the spectrum,

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:03.740
they're going to be impacted

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:06.110
on a social, communication level,

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:07.563
on an executive functioning level.

00:01:07.563 --> 00:01:08.940
- What is the spectrum mean?

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:12.070
- The spectrum means somebody
can be impacted minimally,

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:14.240
somebody can be impacted extensively.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.490
- Where does Collin kind of fall on that?

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:17.080
- He's considered high-functioning.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:18.410
But it's kind of a misnomer.

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:19.590
Even though they're high-functioning

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:21.290
and very able in certain areas,

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:22.510
they still may be challenged.

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:24.910
Maybe in an emergency,
or to defend themselves,

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:25.973
or to express.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.010
- How was Collin diagnosed with autism?

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:29.950
- When he was about two and a half

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:32.720
I took him to a state agency.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.040
They only assessed him for delayed speech,

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.950
and as a new parent, that's the hardest,

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:40.570
most difficult path to be
denied he even has a diagnosis.

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:43.500
And then the school district
declined all services

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:44.990
because he did not have autism.

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:46.810
That was really a difficult time.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.660
After a year, researched a lot,

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.370
and I noticed other behaviors.

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:51.760
Finally, took him to a psychologist

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:53.777
who did diagnose him at the age of four.

00:01:53.777 --> 00:01:55.770
- [Kane] Why is it important
to diagnose it earlier?

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:58.810
- When caught young, their
brain is truly rewiring

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:00.520
on a minute by minute basis.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.580
If you can use that momentum of growth

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:05.530
to remediate sensory processing issues,

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:08.520
eating issues, balance
issues, motor skills,

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.150
those are things that
are just a big challenge

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:12.563
for the autism community.

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.187
- Then Melina gave me a tour of her space

00:02:15.187 --> 00:02:17.250
and I got to hang out with Collin a bit.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:19.860
- This is where Collin really
enjoys watching the Lakers

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:20.920
and the Dodger games.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:23.190
- What kinds of things
do you do in this area?

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:27.123
- I go on the iPad, and
watch TV, I watch YouTube.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.810
- What percentage of time do you think

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:30.460
Collin spends in this area.
- Oh my,

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:33.023
I would say this is 85% of his day.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:35.148
- Where's your favorite
spot in this living room?

00:02:35.148 --> 00:02:37.523
- The sofa right there.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:39.893
I like how it's comfy.
- Yeah.

00:02:40.112 --> 00:02:41.280
- The minute he gets home from school,

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.930
is to take off the shoes and lay down.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.190
- [Kane] What made you decide
to have such a big sectional?

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:48.300
- Collin is almost six
feet, he needs space.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.133
- That's good to know.

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:50.310
- Well this table's interesting.

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:51.963
- Whoa.
- It raises nicely.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.540
And it also stores.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.790
We don't quite need this
table as much as we did

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:56.623
when they were younger.

00:02:56.623 --> 00:02:59.140
The wall unit is your traditional piece

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:02.280
where all your CDs, and
DVDs, and books go in.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:05.462
This nook used to be where
we would store bicycles.

00:03:05.462 --> 00:03:07.030
- You see kind of--
- The bike tires.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:08.710
And this space isn't that large either.

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:10.140
It would be great if it was used

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.400
for something in particular.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.540
Its not been the easiest to figure it out.

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:15.910
- You said that you were into meditation

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:16.930
and things like that?

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.060
- I'm teaching him a little bit

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.380
of the stillness of the mind.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:22.190
Using essential oils, I've
seen really nice impact

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:23.023
on Collin.

00:03:23.023 --> 00:03:25.663
I constantly have New Age
and soothing music on.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:28.610
This particular area is very challenging.

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:31.520
It's in between two doors, so
you have a very small corner.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.220
- [Kane] Are there any
particular things in here

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:34.760
that you for sure wanna keep?

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:35.837
- [Melina] No (laughs).

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:37.303
- Okay.

00:03:37.303 --> 00:03:38.260
- [Melina] Really enjoy, Collin and I,

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:39.950
playing in this room is Smash Ball.

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:41.573
We've gotten really good at it.

00:03:42.049 --> 00:03:43.528
(rock music)

00:03:43.528 --> 00:03:47.030
(laughing) Good job.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:48.070
Try it one more time, Kane.

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:50.143
- Okay, one more time.
- Nice and easy.

00:03:51.167 --> 00:03:52.000
Good!

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:52.833
(laughing)

00:03:52.833 --> 00:03:53.813
- [Kane] It's like ping pong kind of.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.450
After getting a tour of the living room,

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:57.610
I wanted to see if I might be able to help

00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:58.700
with Collin's bedroom.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.310
- The space isn't too big.

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:02.630
I don't know quite where to put this bed

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.100
in terms of direction.

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.110
The blinds were here, they're fairly old.

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:07.830
They've been with us since we moved here.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:09.620
Now that he's 21, trying to figure out

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.330
for an adult, what's the best for him.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:12.885
- I like the color a lot.
- Oh good.

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:13.718
- Of the wall.

00:04:13.718 --> 00:04:14.980
What's your favorite color?
- Blue.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:16.790
- [Melina] He's great with
blue, yeah, he chose it.

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:17.623
- It's very calming.

00:04:17.623 --> 00:04:19.740
I'm taking some wide
photos so I can draw on it.

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:21.670
When's the last time you redid this space?

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:23.670
- I would say about eight to 10 years ago.

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:25.160
The boys' taste, they're older now,

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:27.520
I would like to sort of
inject their adult-ness

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:28.723
into the space.

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:30.690
- Are there things you're afraid of?

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:31.523
- Protecting himself.

00:04:31.523 --> 00:04:33.010
That has to be one of my biggest fears

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:34.600
is him being taken advantage.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:36.820
You can teach them, but
you can't be ensured.

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:39.900
Even though he has the most
traditional forms of autism,

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:41.269
he's still so thoughtful.

00:04:41.269 --> 00:04:42.370
- What are some of the best things

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:43.430
that you've learned from him?

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:45.140
- The most important thing he taught me

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:46.520
was what's important, sincerely.

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:48.370
- Which is?
- It's all in the heart.

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:50.860
It's just so easy to get bummed out.

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:54.113
I mean, it's a devastating
diagnosis for any parent.

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:55.560
He doesn't think so much about tomorrow.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:56.890
He thinks a lot about now.

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:58.650
And the times and the years that I forgot,

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:01.000
he taught me how to bring
it back to the heart.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:04.550
If you didn't decide,
instead of being devastated,

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:07.720
you're gonna shift into being
thankful no matter what,

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:10.563
it really can be a journey
of your own growth.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.650
- What are some cool
things about your mom?

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:15.560
- She's kind and helpful.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:17.830
- Now that he's older,
at a vocational school,

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.510
I'd like to transform this space.

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:21.643
More matches where he's at in life.

00:05:21.803 --> 00:05:23.210
(upbeat music)

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:24.670
- After getting a tour of Melina's home,

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:26.760
taking a few photos, and getting a feel

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.120
for the family's vibe, and
what they really needed,

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:29.953
and I got to work.

00:05:29.953 --> 00:05:31.950
I usually like to draw out potential ideas

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:33.550
to see what I could do with a space.

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:35.500
The first thing you see when
entering the living room

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.800
is a giant TV wall unit.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:40.400
It's big, it's heavy, and very 90s.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:42.920
My aunts and uncles totally had this

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:43.810
in their living room.

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:44.800
Feels very heavy.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:47.040
I wanted an unassuming TV console,

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:48.780
just enough to hold their electronics

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:51.040
and found a great one
in a darker wood tone

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:51.873
from Home Goods.

00:05:51.873 --> 00:05:54.100
It features a unique, sliding barn door

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:55.190
that makes it stand out.

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:56.540
I wanted to mount the TV.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:58.960
The TV was actually really light in weight

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.690
and the pros from Handy.com

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:02.320
hung it up securely on the wall.

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:03.820
Just like a piece of art work.

00:06:05.715 --> 00:06:08.930
Since Collin clearly loves,
loves, loves his couch,

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.590
I didn't want to swap it out

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:12.370
in case he didn't like
how the new one felt.

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:15.160
But the shade of brown
really made the couch feel

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:16.510
way older than it was.

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:19.600
So I wanted to change the color
to gray with couch covers.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:22.200
I found really great ones
from Bed, Bath &amp; Beyond.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.780
They worked really well for
two of the sectional pieces.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.870
I didn't realize how extra long

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:28.620
the third sectional piece would be.

00:06:28.975 --> 00:06:29.808
Uh oh.

00:06:29.808 --> 00:06:31.210
- [Man] Uh oh, what's going on Kane?

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:32.223
- This is too small.

00:06:32.243 --> 00:06:34.280
(upbeat music)

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:36.643
The coffee table they
had felt really heavy,

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.070
kind of like a giant brick.

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:39.920
I wanted to swap it out for a sleeker one,

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:42.200
in a darker tone, with
minimal compartments.

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:44.193
I found the perfect one at Z Gallerie.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:46.050
It looks so good, and it's functional

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.610
with drawers for board
games, art supplies,

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:49.900
and remote controls.

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:51.680
Only two pieces of furniture are in

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:53.240
and I'm already super excited.

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:55.770
The blinds also feel pretty outdated here.

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:58.620
So I'm gonna swap these out
for a row of teal curtains

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:00.800
over a set of sheer, white curtains.

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:03.660
I found beautiful ones, along
with sturdy curtain rods,

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:05.043
from T.J. Maxx.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:06.793
Halfway through the day,

00:07:06.793 --> 00:07:08.610
it dawned on me that none of the lamps

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:10.430
I had ordered online were here.

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.400
We can't find the six lamps.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:13.550
They were supposed to be delivered.

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:15.730
They're all perfectly
chosen for this space.

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:17.720
Otherwise I have to run
out and go pick some lamps.

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:20.070
Somehow I thought that they
still might arrive today.

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:22.040
So we just kept moving,
hoping for the best.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.340
For this little nook area,

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:25.840
Melina had no idea what
she wanted to do with it.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:28.190
After she mentioned her
interest in meditation,

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:30.770
I knew right away I wanted to surprise her

00:07:30.770 --> 00:07:32.480
with a little meditation area.

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:34.470
I wanted a little accent wall here.

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:36.700
It's the same wallpaper we
used for Freddie's bedroom

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:37.853
from Chasing Paper.

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:40.750
I wanted to paint over
all the bike tire marks

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:42.030
and scratches on the walls,

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:44.423
so the room could be reset and renewed.

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:45.630
At this point in the day,

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:47.790
I realized that none of
the lamps would be coming.

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:48.970
I checked the tracking,

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:50.970
the lamps aren't coming 'till tomorrow.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:53.130
If you know me, you know I love lamps.

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:56.040
And there was no way I was
gonna reveal the living space

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:58.100
to the family without the proper lighting.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:00.750
I decided to find brand
new lamps from scratch.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:02.280
So I explained as quickly as I could

00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:03.950
what I wanted so they could work on it

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:04.923
while I was gone.

00:08:05.890 --> 00:08:08.047
I don't usually panic, I'm not a panicker.

00:08:08.047 --> 00:08:09.823
I'm slightly panicking right now.

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:14.200
I just want it to be perfect for them.

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:23.690
Somehow by a true miracle I found

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:26.090
all the lamps I wanted from T.J. Maxx.

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:28.880
I'm so happy, I feel
better, I feel better,

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:30.707
I got lamps, I got lamps.

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:33.880
I also asked the Handy.com pros

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:36.220
to help put wallpaper
above the couch wall.

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:37.850
I picked out a white wallpaper

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:40.460
with a soft, leaf design from Wayfair.com.

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:42.830
I wanted to brighten up the
space while keeping it cute.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:45.580
They helped me cut the pieces
to the right sizes to put up.

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:47.100
They called me and said that the wallpaper

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:48.100
didn't have adhesive.

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:50.350
Which is different from
the wallpaper that I used

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:52.830
for Freddie's bedroom
and that was a lot easier

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:54.120
just to like peel off.

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:56.060
When I got back, we were down to the wire.

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:57.260
While I was out getting lamps,

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:58.730
I picked up a spray on adhesive

00:08:58.730 --> 00:09:00.230
for the living room wallpaper.

00:09:02.247 --> 00:09:04.040
(intense music)

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:05.840
While I was out, I found a giant,

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:08.480
nine by 14 feet, gray fabric sheet

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:10.360
for the long side of the sectional sofa.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:11.950
I wanna do a side table here

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:14.530
to create a small gap
between the sectional pieces.

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:16.470
I found a cute, lightweight side table

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:18.620
to break up the giant sectional feel.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:20.730
I wanna put a tall plant
in the back corner,

00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:23.170
one on the side table, and
one on the coffee table.

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:25.410
I found really awesome fake plants

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:26.970
of all kinds at Marshalls.

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:29.973
I had no idea they even
sold fake plants there.

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:33.330
You can tell how happy I was.

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:34.233
Just a tree.

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:40.040
I wanna put a giant rug
here to help break up

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:41.170
all the tan carpeting.

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:43.780
It was kinda hard to find
rugs at the size I wanted,

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:46.370
but eventually I found the
perfect, light blue one.

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:49.710
I wanna put a tall lamp here
and one on the side table

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:51.470
which will sit next to a Google Home

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:52.813
which I got from Best Buy.

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:55.593
For the couch pillows, I
went with shades of blue.

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:58.210
I got the piece of artwork
here from T.J. Maxx,

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:00.610
which, again, are different
shades of blue and green

00:10:00.610 --> 00:10:03.723
to emphasize the theme and
to tie it all back together.

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:07.790
So for the rest of the meditation area,

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:10.060
I wanna put a big piece of artwork here.

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:11.630
I found one from T.J. Maxx

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:13.643
that reminded me so much of Melina.

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:17.990
I want the meditation area
to have a bit of privacy,

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:19.210
so I want a curtain here.

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:21.270
I went with a white, sheer-ish curtain

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:22.540
with teal accents.

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:24.960
This way, the color would
still match the living room

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:26.920
and the slightly more ornate design

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:29.020
would match the vibe
of the mediation area.

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:30.400
For the rest of the mediation area

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:33.053
I wanted two, serene-looking lamps here,

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:35.233
fake plants on either side,

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:37.423
and a very soft rug.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.370
I went with a few eclectic pillows

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:43.363
in burgundy, gold, and magenta.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:47.450
So for this corner of the room,

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:50.060
Melina had no idea what
she wanted to do with it.

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:52.610
I noticed that it was
kind of the perfect place

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:53.500
to put a desk.

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:55.920
I found one that I really
liked from The Container Store.

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:58.680
It was a darker tone and
would match the coffee table

00:10:58.680 --> 00:10:59.763
and TV console.

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:01.570
On it would be a lamp and a plant,

00:11:01.570 --> 00:11:04.240
another plant on the floor
to help fill up the space,

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:05.800
a piece of artwork here,

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:07.610
one with a message that, again,

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:09.893
reminded me so much of Melina.

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:12.580
Maybe a mirror here,

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:15.110
this way it would reflect
the big sliding glass door

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:16.810
across the room to create an illusion

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:19.123
that maybe it could be an actual window.

00:11:24.305 --> 00:11:25.705
- [Man] What are you
looking forward to the most?

00:11:25.705 --> 00:11:26.538
(laughs)

00:11:26.538 --> 00:11:28.730
- We are looking forward
to the transformation.

00:11:28.815 --> 00:11:31.650
Are you anxious, honey, about
what they might change it to?

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:33.730
- I'm just excited.
- Yeah.

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:35.560
- So moving on to Collin's bedroom.

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:38.750
Melina really wanted to
make it feel more adult.

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:41.810
Since the baby blue walls
were so attention grabbing,

00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:44.010
I didn't want to add
too many other colors.

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:47.300
It would either clash or
make it feel more childlike.

00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:49.840
So I got this soft,
light gray duvet cover,

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:52.650
fluffy pillows, and
matching, gray pillow cases

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:53.950
from Bed, Bath &amp; Beyond.

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:55.250
I wanna center the bed,

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:57.673
put two wooden night
stands on either side,

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:00.193
lamps on top of the night stands,

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:01.873
plants on either side also.

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:05.540
I want maybe a headboard here.

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:07.190
I ended up getting a big sticker

00:12:07.190 --> 00:12:10.100
with wood graphic on it
for an illusion headboard.

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:12.700
And it ended up matching
the nightstands really well.

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:14.060
Some kind of artwork here.

00:12:14.060 --> 00:12:15.480
I got a thin, white mirror

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:17.040
'cause it just looked really peaceful.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:19.130
And it paired well with
some of the white pillows

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:19.963
on the bed.

00:12:19.963 --> 00:12:22.193
Of course, I wanna remove
the blinds here also.

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:24.340
Swapping it out for neutral, gray curtains

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:25.653
to match the gray bedding.

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:27.530
I also layered the gray curtains

00:12:27.530 --> 00:12:29.443
over the row of sheer, white curtains.

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:32.283
And a very soft gray rug here.

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:35.690
This drawer I'm moving against
the wall with the window

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:37.200
to open up the walkway a bit.

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:39.880
I wanna put a lamp here, and a plant,

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:41.240
leave up some of the trophies.

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:43.650
In all the lamps, I put in color-changing

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:45.300
Philips Hue light bulbs.

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:47.470
This way they can either control
the lights on their phone

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:49.070
or they can control it through their voice

00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:50.550
by the Google Home I picked up.

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:51.730
This corner's a little dark,

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:53.620
so I'm gonna put Philips Hue bloom

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:55.470
like a fancy restaurant or something.

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:00.700
Last minute, trying to
put everything together.

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:02.150
Gonna start going into place.

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:04.700
Lastly, before the reveal to the family,

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:07.100
Collin has a few piles of books

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:09.200
and other knick knacks throughout his room

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:10.900
and I wanted a place for him to put it.

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:12.990
So I picked up two, sea foam colored,

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:15.340
storage ottomans for him to put books in.

00:13:15.340 --> 00:13:17.700
And this way it could also
double as seating for his room.

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:18.893
It's coming together.

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:20.173
It's looking good.

00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:24.330
These guys are from Handy, good job, guys.

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:25.460
It looks amazing.

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:27.230
So after running around all day,

00:13:27.230 --> 00:13:29.500
right now I'm about to
reveal the living space

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:31.700
for the very first time to Melina

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:33.420
and her two sons, Collin and Brendan.

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:35.140
I really hope they like it.

00:13:35.140 --> 00:13:36.970
Alright, come down.
- Okay, guys?

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:38.653
- Come on, check it out!

00:13:39.490 --> 00:13:40.323
- Wow.

00:13:40.448 --> 00:13:42.198
- [Melina] (laughs) Oh my goodness!

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:44.470
- [Kane] This is your new living room.

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.780
- Wow Kane, I'm really impressed.

00:13:47.595 --> 00:13:49.396
(upbeat music)

00:13:49.396 --> 00:13:50.720
Kane!
- Like this desk right here?

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:52.010
- Look at that corner over there.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:54.460
It makes it seem like it's
in another room entirely.

00:13:54.460 --> 00:13:56.870
And even though you can use
them for different things,

00:13:56.870 --> 00:13:58.110
they belong in the same place.

00:13:58.110 --> 00:13:59.750
It's really nice the way the flow is.

00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:01.010
It's just really cool.

00:14:01.010 --> 00:14:03.730
Can't wait to use the desk
for all kinds of things.

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:05.130
- [Kane] This is a surprise.

00:14:07.993 --> 00:14:09.403
This is like a meditation area.

00:14:09.403 --> 00:14:11.303
- [Brendan] Yeah, feel these curtains.

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:13.113
This is a really cozy spot.

00:14:13.113 --> 00:14:15.946
(Melina laughing)

00:14:16.383 --> 00:14:19.044
- [Kane] You can put your incense
and aromatherapy in there.

00:14:19.044 --> 00:14:19.877
- [Brendan] That's cool.

00:14:19.877 --> 00:14:21.677
- Buddy, wasn't this great?
- Yeah.

00:14:22.598 --> 00:14:23.833
- [Melina] This is like a lair's den!

00:14:23.833 --> 00:14:25.090
- [Brendan] You can
just close the curtains

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:25.960
and chill right here.

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:28.010
- A lot of people want a space

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:32.130
that is cozy and yet not very stimulating.

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:34.880
- [Kane] I know that you have
tons of books in your rooms.

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:37.050
This could be like a
little reading corner,

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:38.070
more meditation.

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:40.470
- [Melina] Brendan, you can
come just lay down and read.

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:42.010
- See how it's pink now?
- Oh!

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:43.471
- Oh dang.
- Look at that!

00:14:43.471 --> 00:14:44.304
What do you think Collin?

00:14:44.304 --> 00:14:45.910
Look at the pink lights behind you.

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:47.110
Isn't that neat?
- Yes.

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:49.420
- [Brendan] The pattern right
here on the wall, the leaves.

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:50.280
That's pretty cool.

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:51.113
Can I lay down?

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:52.243
- Yeah.

00:14:52.243 --> 00:14:53.803
This is your new living room (laughs).

00:14:53.803 --> 00:14:55.280
- [Melina] This is great, Kane.

00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:56.660
- What's your favorite spot?

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:58.123
- The sofa.
- Yeah?

00:14:58.190 --> 00:14:59.750
- Yes.
- That's your favorite corner

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:01.150
over there so I wanted to make sure

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:02.470
I kept it the same.

00:15:02.470 --> 00:15:04.090
- [Brendan] The desk
is level with the sofa,

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:04.970
I like that.
- Yeah.

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:07.030
- [Kane] A little more light
with the bottom cleared.

00:15:07.030 --> 00:15:08.910
- You got the dimensions perfectly.

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:10.290
- [Brendan] Got the TV right here.

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:11.167
I like the wall set up.

00:15:11.167 --> 00:15:14.030
- [Melina] And the colors
are perfectly stimulating

00:15:14.136 --> 00:15:15.660
and very, very soothing.

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:16.850
- [Kane] You guys like blue a lot,

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:18.393
so I wanted to go off that color tone.

00:15:18.393 --> 00:15:20.160
- [Melina] And I love the artwork.

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:21.260
You got it just right.

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:22.650
- [Kane] And then some
of these artworks, too,

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:24.050
they reminded me a lot of what you said

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:24.930
during the interview.

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:26.590
I wanted to create a comfortable space

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:28.832
for you to maybe play board games again--

00:15:28.832 --> 00:15:29.665
- Cards.
- Spend more

00:15:29.665 --> 00:15:30.830
family time together.

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:33.670
- Play in the yard and
come in and just relax.

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:36.170
You really used everything that was here

00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:37.610
and you made it functional.

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:38.650
- Let's go check out Collin's room.

00:15:38.650 --> 00:15:41.403
- Yeah.
- We still have more to see.

00:15:43.490 --> 00:15:45.943
- [Melina] Oh my goodness.

00:15:47.240 --> 00:15:48.073
- Oh wow.

00:15:48.479 --> 00:15:49.490
(Melina laughing)

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:50.323
I'm jealous.

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:53.793
- [Melina] This is another transformation!

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:55.970
The blue now really stands out,

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:58.930
because you have the perfect
colors of white and brown.

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:00.060
How do you like it Col?

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:01.013
- [Collin] It's good.

00:16:01.013 --> 00:16:02.243
- [Melina] It's great, huh?

00:16:02.243 --> 00:16:03.076
- [Collin] Yeah.

00:16:03.076 --> 00:16:04.200
- This is a very small room

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:06.333
and you made it look like a master almost.

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:08.470
And I love the way you can walk all around

00:16:08.470 --> 00:16:10.666
and there's not that big
dresser that was in the way.

00:16:10.666 --> 00:16:12.116
- Put it there in the corner,

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:13.550
get a walk way right here.

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:16.863
- [Kane] Yeah, what do you feel?

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:18.723
- I feel glad!

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:21.100
- [Melina] You know how to
put this together, mister.

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:22.520
- [Kane] Yeah, there's more storage space

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:25.230
in the ottomans and the nightstands, too.

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:26.880
- [Melina] Wonderful items here.

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:28.330
- [Brendan] Yeah the plants, too.

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:30.360
- And the lighting, it warms up the spot.

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:31.980
- [Kane] And this one is also controllable

00:16:31.980 --> 00:16:33.670
so you can change it to different colors,

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:35.013
whatever you're feeling.

00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:36.540
- [Brendan] The transparent curtains.

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:38.590
- [Kane] He can cover it
completely if he wanted to

00:16:38.590 --> 00:16:39.760
or just like have a little bit

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:40.900
of light coming through.

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:41.873
- Different vibe.

00:16:42.490 --> 00:16:43.930
How do the curtains make you feel, honey?

00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:44.763
- Good.

00:16:46.333 --> 00:16:47.873
- [Kane] The rug is very soft, too.

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:50.550
- Yeah wow, I think it looks comfortable.

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:51.930
- [Kane] Feel these pillows, Collin.

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:52.940
They're so soft.

00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:53.773
- [Brendan] That's soft.

00:16:53.773 --> 00:16:54.760
- [Melina] Almost like a cottage.

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:55.790
- [Kane] Yeah, and the wood's like

00:16:55.790 --> 00:16:57.080
a little bit more mature.

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:58.430
- [Melina] I love this headboard, Kane.

00:16:58.430 --> 00:16:59.730
- [Kane] And it's sticker.

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:01.680
(Melina laughing)

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:02.987
But you can't even tell.

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:04.483
- The mirror up there,

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:06.560
boy does it perfectly compliments the bed.

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:08.590
Really balances, this is just right.

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:09.680
- Yeah.
- Are you gonna spend

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:10.980
more time in here?
- Yes.

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:12.930
- Alright, I'd like to see that.

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:15.920
Brendan graduating and Collin
will be going to vocation,

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:19.140
and our whole lives are really
kinda going into adulthood.

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:21.050
And yet, we wanna be together.

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:24.240
So you've given us a great,
developed, mature space

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:26.113
so thank you for all your hard work.

00:17:26.365 --> 00:17:27.948
I so appreciate it.

00:17:28.406 --> 00:17:29.736
Thank all of you.

00:17:29.736 --> 00:17:31.327
- Thank you, Collin.
- Good seeing you.

00:17:31.327 --> 00:17:32.160
- Thank you so much.

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:34.823
What do you hope for 20
to 30 years from now?

00:17:34.823 --> 00:17:37.350
- What I hope for for Collin in his future

00:17:37.350 --> 00:17:40.280
is the same that I hope
for my neurotypical son.

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:44.420
I want him to feel confident
in seeking out his own path.

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:46.210
No one has a perfect life,

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:48.110
but that's something that's
very meaningful to me.

00:17:48.110 --> 00:17:51.663
Is that he gets to choose the
same way we all get to choose.

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:54.993
I just wanna keep
equipping him in that way.

00:17:54.993 --> 00:17:57.500
- I think we all put in a lot of sweat,

00:17:57.500 --> 00:17:59.770
and energy, and muscle.

00:17:59.770 --> 00:18:02.970
Honestly, just seeing Collin excited

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:05.310
and jumping on his rug,

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:07.040
really made it all worth it.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:10.530
The family seemed so
excited, feeling renewed,

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:12.620
and that's always the goal at home.

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:14.180
You're trying to recharge.

00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:16.770
Can't wait to see how they experience it

00:18:16.770 --> 00:18:19.020
throughout the week,
and months, and years.

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:20.870
- Really have impacted our life here.

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:22.033
- Until next time.

00:18:22.340 --> 00:18:24.333
Rest well, you deserve it.

00:18:24.348 --> 00:18:27.265
(electronic music)

